      "handle": "bayesiansapien",
      "creator": "@TheTuringPost",
      "text": "An interesting attention mechanism from @AIatMeta : SP-KV (Self-Pruned Key-Value Attention) The model learns which tokens are likely to be useful for future attention and only keeps their key-value pairs in the persistent KV cache. For every token and attention head, a small utility predictor (a 2-layer MLP) computes a utility score, and older tokens are selectively pruned based on it. At the same time, attention becomes hybrid, because SP-KV still keeps a local sliding window fully available for short-range interactions This approach: - reduces KV cache size by about 3× to 10× - allows to com",
      "link": "https://nitter.net/TheTuringPost/status/2055828260542644463#m",
